    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>One-week review of left ankle and hindfoot pain, seen the same day by orthopaedic foot and ankle surgery. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Sitting Bull returns one week after intake, with the interpreter, and is seen the same day by Dr. Holmquist-Ellery, the visiting orthopaedic foot and ankle surgeon. He had the CT of his left foot this morning. His pain is unchanged at 7 of 10 on walking; the diclofenac gel helps a little. His home blood pressure readings over the past week average 124/78 mmHg. Blood count, kidney function, C-reactive protein and sedimentation rate at intake were normal, and his hemoglobin A1c was 6.0%. The CT shows arthritis of two joints below the ankle and four small metal fragments in the heel, none in a joint or bone; a point-of-care blood lead test today is 2.4 ug/dL. He wants to hear every option before he decides anything, and he does not want surgery now. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pain</td><td>7 of 10 on walking</td></tr><tr><td>CT</td><td>Post-traumatic arthritis of the posterior subtalar and talonavicular joints; four small extra-articular metal fragments</td></tr><tr><td>Blood lead</td><td>2.4 ug/dL</td></tr><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Average 124/78 mmHg over seven days</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Foot and Ankle Ability Measure, daily activities, 52%</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Left hindfoot pain and morning stiffness; no other joint pain</td></tr><tr><td>Integumentary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No drainage or redness at the old wound</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No numbness, tingling or weakness in the foot</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No abdominal pain; no stomach trouble in the past</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

